# The API this client talks to.
#
# DEVELOPMENT: the backend runs on :3000 while Vite serves this app on :4200,
# so they are different origins and the backend must allowlist :4200 in
# CORS_ORIGINS. The session cookie still travels — SameSite=Strict is about
# the SITE, and both ports are localhost.
#
# PRODUCTION: leave EMPTY. The client is served from the same origin as the
# API, which is why CORS is off there and why same-origin is the shape the
# backend targets.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Google Maps Platform BROWSER key, used only on the backoffice "add / edit
# location" dialog: place search, the map, and a draggable pin. The driver
# portal never loads it, and the server never sees it — the driver's GPS is
# checked by the backend's own haversine against the saved coordinates.
#
# EMPTY (the default) turns the map off and the dialog falls back to typing
# the coordinates by hand. Nothing else changes.
#
# It ships in the bundle, as every Maps JavaScript key does, so it is
# protected in the Google console rather than by secrecy:
#   Application restriction  HTTP referrers — this deployment's origin(s) only
#   API restriction          Maps JavaScript API, Places API (New) — nothing else
# Never a server key, never a key with billing-sensitive APIs enabled, and
# never committed: put it in .env (ignored) or the build environment.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
